<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamamatsu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamamatsu is a city in western Shizuoka Prefecture, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the Pacific coast of the former province of Totomi. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> moved his base there in 1570 and rebuilt its castle, holding it through his wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a> until he moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunpu">Sunpu</a> in 1586. In modern times it became an industrial centre known for musical instruments and motorcycles, home to Yamaha and Suzuki.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamamatsu.jpg" alt="Hamamatsu" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saigen Jiro · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamamatsu_Castle,_enkei-3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
